flowchart TD
    App["Application<br/><b>does:</b> calls socket(..., IPPROTO_MPTCP)<br/><b>why next:</b> explicit opt-in requests MPTCP<br/><b>state:</b> app still sees one SOCK_STREAM"]
    Msk["MPTCP master socket (msk)<br/><b>does:</b> owns the app-visible byte stream<br/><b>why next:</b> needs TCP subflows to carry bytes<br/><b>state:</b> Data Sequence Number space"]
    Primary["Primary subflow<br/><b>does:</b> TCP connection with MP_CAPABLE<br/><b>why next:</b> proves peer supports MPTCP<br/><b>state:</b> token/key identify the MPTCP connection"]
    PM["Path manager<br/><b>does:</b> uses endpoints and peer ADD_ADDR info<br/><b>why next:</b> decides when another path should join<br/><b>state:</b> candidate addresses/subflow limits"]
    Join["Additional subflow<br/><b>does:</b> MP_JOIN creates another TCP connection<br/><b>why next:</b> scheduler can now choose among paths<br/><b>state:</b> multiple TCP cwnds/RTTs"]
    Sched["MPTCP scheduler<br/><b>does:</b> picks a subflow for new data using current path state<br/><b>why next:</b> selected subflow has usable window/pacing<br/><b>state:</b> bytes assigned to one TCP subflow"]
    DSS["DSS mapping<br/><b>does:</b> maps subflow sequence numbers to msk DSNs<br/><b>why next:</b> receiver can reorder/deduplicate<br/><b>state:</b> original byte stream reconstructed"]
    AppRecv["Application reads<br/><b>state:</b> one ordered stream, despite many TCP paths"]

    TcpOnly["Ordinary IPPROTO_TCP socket<br/><b>state:</b> stays plain TCP unless a selective tool/BPF hook remaps it"]

    App --> Msk --> Primary --> PM --> Join --> Sched --> DSS --> AppRecv
    Primary --> Sched
    App -. no opt-in .-> TcpOnly

    classDef app fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb
    classDef sub fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706
    classDef mptcp fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a
    classDef note fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#6b7280
    class App,AppRecv app
    class Primary,Join sub
    class Msk,PM,Sched,DSS mptcp
    class TcpOnly note
